# Rust
# Cargo.lock is committed (even though this is a library) for reproducible CI:
# builds fail only on our own commits, never on a bad transitive upstream release.
# Consumers are unaffected — Cargo.lock does not propagate to downstream crates.
/target

# Environment secrets (protect all .env variants except template)
.env*
!.env.template

# IDE
.idea/
*.iml

# Private project files (not for public fork)
CLAUDE.md
docs/
.claude/
.directory

# MEGAsync local trash (this repo is a MEGAsync sync root)
.debris/

# Provider-sourced market data must never be committed to this public repository.
# Databento licenses per subscriber and its User Agreement prohibits "Redistribution" —
# publishing or furnishing covered data to anyone other than the Customer — without prior
# written approval from both Databento and the relevant exchange:
# https://databento.com/legal/databento-user-agreement
# `download_databento_fixtures` writes here; the offline tests generate synthetic DBN instead.
local-data/

# This path held committed Databento (CME GLBX.MDP3) captures until they were replaced by
# synthetic fixtures generated in-test. Kept ignored so they cannot drift back in.
rustrade-data/tests/fixtures/databento/
